# SPDX-License-Identifier: PMPL-1.0-or-later
# Dustfile — Cleanup and Hygiene Contract
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>

@abstract:
Cleanup and reversibility invariants for the developer-ecosystem monorepo.
These ensure the repo stays tidy and changes can be undone.
@end

## Cleanup

### stale-branch-policy
- description: Branches should be deleted after merge
- policy: delete-after-merge
- severity: info

### artifact-retention
- description: CI artifacts retained for 90 days max
- policy: 90-days
- severity: info

### no-build-artifacts
- description: No compiled artifacts committed to source
- run: "! find v-ecosystem -name '*.o' -o -name '*.so' -o -name '*.a' 2>/dev/null | head -1 | grep -q ."
- severity: warning

### no-stray-scm-files
- description: No legacy .scm checkpoint files (migrated to .a2ml)
- run: "! find .machine_readable -name '*.scm' -not -name 'bot_directives' 2>/dev/null | head -1 | grep -q ."
- severity: warning

## Hygiene

### formatting-required
- description: V source files should be v fmt compliant
- policy: required
- severity: warning

### dead-code-removal
- description: Unused modules and imports should be removed
- policy: encouraged
- severity: info

### todo-tracking
- description: TODO comments should reference issues or be time-bounded
- policy: tracked-in-issues
- severity: info

## Reversibility

### backup-before-destructive
- description: Destructive operations require confirmation
- policy: true
- severity: warning

### rollback-mechanism
- description: All changes reversible via git revert
- policy: git-revert
- severity: info

### data-retention
- description: Preserve data for 30 days before permanent deletion
- policy: preserve-30-days
- severity: info
